[step] Intentional shallow screw-head seats. Each socket head rests on the flat annular floor below the retainer face; the remaining head projects as drawn. This is the fastener-bearing surface.
alternatives: Removing the recess loses the positive head seat. A deeper recess reduces the side wall and buries the head. A taper requires different screw hardware.
